---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How danieltse.org handles lightweight, aggregate website analytics."
>
  <section class="page-lead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Minimal analytics, no advertising profile.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead-summary">
      This is a public technical publication. It does not use advertising trackers, analytics
      cookies, or persistent visitor identifiers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block section-block--quiet">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses GoatCounter to understand aggregate visits, referrers, and a small set of
        named interactions such as repository, documentation, demo, profile, and RSS clicks. Event
        names contain only static labels and project slugs. They do not contain form input or other
        visitor-supplied values.
      </p>
      <p>
        GoatCounter does not place analytics cookies or write analytics identifiers to local
        storage. According to GoatCounter, IP addresses and full user-agent strings are used
        transiently in memory for session counting and are not persisted to its database or disk.
        Aggregate reports may include page paths, referrers, country, browser, operating system,
        language, and screen width.
      </p>
      <p>
        Browsers that send Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track are not measured by this site's
        analytics integration. GoatCounter's individual-pageview collection remains disabled.
      </p>

      <h2>Data handling</h2>
      <p>
        GoatCounter states that hosted analytics data is processed on servers in Finland and
        Germany and is not shared with third parties. Its full practices and deletion terms are
        described in the
        <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">
          GoatCounter privacy policy
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions can be sent through
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danieltse/" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">
          LinkedIn
        </a>.
      </p>

      <p><small>Last updated: 10 July 2026.</small></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
